# Conformance probe pack for ruling 9 of 0.56: a `switch` key that wraps is
# predicted as wrapped, most significant bit first. Public. No kinds.
#   presence p 8 | if p.1: x 8 (default 12, wraps to 2) | case 2: if p.1: y 8
# Both outcomes are stable: case 2 opens the block whose default selects case 2;
# `else` opens nothing, and an absent x selects `else`.
format  conformance-range-056-11
version 0.56.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses    probe
wire    bits
layout  sequential
bit_order msb
presence p 8
if p.1
  field  probe.x  8  uint  range 0 10 wrap
end
switch probe.x
  case 2
    if p.1
      field  probe.y  8  uint
    end
  else
end
default probe.x  12
